# ===========================================================================
# PaheBatcher for Android - .gitignore (project-specific, hardened 2026-10-24)
#
# Replaces the generic GitHub Java template that came with the repository
# initialization. Rules are scoped so that source code, tests, the Gradle
# wrapper JAR, documentation, signing.env.example (dummy placeholders only)
# and the approved .opencode/ agent configuration REMAIN TRACKED.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Android / Gradle build outputs (any depth, nested-safe) ---------------
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex

# --- Local environment and IDE data ---------------------------------------
local.properties
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Signing and secrets (never commit) -----------------------------------
# Local signing configuration: real values set by the owner via environment
# variables (PB_*). signing.env.example is tracked - it holds dummy
# placeholders only.
signing.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
keystore.properties
signing.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
# The release keystore itself lives in .private/ (root-anchored).
/.private/

# --- Private investigation / scratch / diagnostics (never publish) ---------
# Pre-publication privacy evidence, frozen logcat captures, media fixtures,
# pre-redaction backups and policy-scan scratch runs.
/.investigation/
/.scratch/
proxies.txt

# --- Logs, crash dumps, temporary data -------------------------------------
*.log
*.hprof
*.tmp
*.temp
*.trace

# NOTE deliberately NOT ignored (must stay trackable):
#   gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar  - no blanket *.jar rule is used
#   .opencode/                          - owner-approved public agent config
#   signing.env.example                 - documented dummy placeholders
